From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 11:13:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] moal: report cached scan results to cfg80211 outside
 scan_req_lock

The fake-completion branch of woal_scan_timeout_handler() -- the one
that answers a scan from the driver's scan table instead of the
firmware -- holds scan_req_lock, an irqsave spinlock, across
woal_inform_bss_from_scan_result(). That hands every BSS to
cfg80211_inform_bss(), which allocates with GFP_KERNEL and takes the
wiphy's bss_lock with local_bh_disable(), so a debug kernel reports
"sleeping function called from invalid context" from the scan timeout
worker.

The firmware-report path, woal_send_cfg_bss_scan_result(), had the same
fault (reported from woal_evt_work_queue) and already reports outside
the lock. Do the same here: take the request under the lock, report
outside it, and complete under it again -- that request only. One
cancelled in between was completed by whoever cancelled it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 mlinux/moal_main.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mlinux/moal_main.c b/mlinux/moal_main.c
index 90a7342..1a62caa 100644
--- a/mlinux/moal_main.c
+++ b/mlinux/moal_main.c
@@ -13734,17 +13734,29 @@ t_void woal_scan_timeout_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 	if (IS_STA_CFG80211(handle->params.cfg80211_wext)) {
 		spin_lock_irqsave(&handle->scan_req_lock, flags);
 		if (handle->scan_request && handle->fake_scan_complete) {
+			struct cfg80211_scan_request *request =
+				handle->scan_request;
+
 			PRINTM(MMSG,
 			       "wlan: Send fake scan result for scan_request %p\n",
-			       handle->scan_request);
+			       request);
+			/* scan_req_lock covers scan_request, and only that.
+			 * cfg80211_inform_bss() allocates every BSS with
+			 * GFP_KERNEL and takes the wiphy's bss_lock with
+			 * local_bh_disable(), neither legal with interrupts
+			 * off. Report outside the lock, then complete the
+			 * request seen here and no other: one cancelled in
+			 * between was completed by whoever cancelled it. */
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&handle->scan_req_lock, flags);
 			if (priv)
 				woal_inform_bss_from_scan_result(priv, NULL,
 								 MOAL_NO_WAIT);
-			if (handle->scan_request)
-				woal_cfg80211_scan_done(handle->scan_request,
-							MFALSE);
-			handle->scan_request = NULL;
-			handle->fake_scan_complete = MFALSE;
+			spin_lock_irqsave(&handle->scan_req_lock, flags);
+			if (handle->scan_request == request) {
+				woal_cfg80211_scan_done(request, MFALSE);
+				handle->scan_request = NULL;
+				handle->fake_scan_complete = MFALSE;
+			}
 			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&handle->scan_req_lock, flags);
 		} else if (handle->scan_request) {
 			PRINTM(MMSG, "wlan: scan timeout!\n");
-- 
